iones de volumen y propiedades espaciales.\n","- Generar múltiples combinaciones aleatorias de segmentos en 3D.\n","- Exportar resultados de intersecciones a archivos CSV.\n","\n","## Metodología\n","\n","**1. Generación de coordenadas:** utilización de NumPy para crear puntos aleatorios y construir segmentos definidos por sus extremos.\n","\n","**2. Visualización bidimensional:** representación de segmentos mediante Matplotlib, identificando sus posiciones y posibles cruces.\n","\n","**3. Análisis de intersecciones:** implementación de cálculos geométricos y determinantes para explorar intersecciones entre pares de líneas.\n","\n","**4. Cálculo de distancias:** aplicación de operaciones matemáticas para estudiar distancias relacionadas con los puntos de intersección.\n","\n","**5. Representación tridimensional:** generación de segmentos definidos por coordenadas X, Y y Z, utilizando gráficos espaciales.\n","\n","**6. Experimentación geométrica:** exploración de estimaciones de volumen, detección de intersecciones tridimensionales y combinaciones aleatorias de segmentos.\n","\n","## Tecnologías utilizadas\n","\n","**Python | NumPy | Matplotlib | Pandas | Jupyter Notebook**\n","\n","## Aplicaciones\n","\n","Los conceptos explorados son fundamentales para la geometría computacional y pueden servir como base para aplicaciones de visualización científica, simulación geométrica, análisis espacial, gráficos por computadora y desarrollo de algoritmos de procesamiento de coordenadas.\n","\n","## Alcances y limitaciones\n","\n","El notebook representa una colección de ejercicios académicos y experimentales. Los procedimientos de intersección tridimensional y estimación de volumen requieren validación matemática adicional, especialmente para distinguir entre rectas infinitas, segmentos finitos y estructuras geométricas cerradas.\n","\n","---\n","\n","**Autor:** Data Engineer Luis Barahona  \n","**Institución:** Universidad del Caribe, México  \n","**GitHub:** [LuisBarahonaMX](https://github.com/LuisBarahonaMX)\n","\n","**Categoría:** Computational Geometry | 2D & 3D Visualization | Numerical Computing | Python"],"metadata":{"id":"2g2wkNTE0VUA"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","def draw_lines(lines):\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\n","    for line in lines:\n","        (x1, y1), (x2, y2) = line\n","        plt.plot([x1, x2], [y1, y2], 'bo-')\n","    plt.xlabel('X')\n","    plt.ylabel('Y')\n","    plt.title('Líneas Aleatorias')\n","    plt.grid(True)\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","def main():\n","    num_lines = int(input(\"Ingrese el número de líneas aleatorias a generar: \"))\n","    lines = []\n","    for i in range(num_lines):\n","        x1, y1, x2, y2 = np.random.rand(4) * 10\n","        lines.append(((x1, y1), (x2, y2)))\n","\n","    draw_lines(lines)\n","\n","if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n","    main()\n","\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":737},"id":"okc0CXo7c5RR","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1713436793046,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":2879,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"}},"outputId":"ede1c1cb-c2b6-4944-f038-94bfb5b58b53"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Ingrese el número de líneas aleatorias a generar: 22\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","#Generación de Líneas Aleatorias y Detección de Intersecciones en 2D\n","\n","##Este código genera un conjunto de líneas aleatorias en un plano 2D y luego detecta y muestra gráficamente las intersecciones entre estas líneas. El usuario puede especificar la cantidad de líneas que se generarán, y cada línea se dibujará entre dos puntos aleatorios en el plano. Además, se calculará el número de intersecciones y se mostrará junto con los puntos de intersección en el gráfico."],"metadata":{"id":"6fizblFh0uw6"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from collections import defaultdict\n","\n","def draw_lines(lines, intersections):\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\n","    for line in lines:\n","        (x1, y1), (x2, y2) = line\n","        plt.plot([x1, x2], [y1, y2], 'bo-')\n","    for intersection in intersections:\n","        plt.plot(intersection[0], intersection[1], 'ro')\n","    plt.xlabel('X')\n","    plt.ylabel('Y')\n","    plt.title('Líneas y Puntos de Intersección')\n","    plt.grid(True)\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","def calculate_intersection(lines):\n","    intersections = []\n","    for i, line1 in enumerate(lines):\n","        for line2 in lines[i+1:]:\n","            xdiff = (line1[0][0] - line1[1][0], line2[0][0] - line2[1][0])\n","            ydiff = (line1[0][1] - line1[1][1], line2[0][1] - line2[1][1])\n","\n","            def det(a, b):\n","                return a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0]\n","\n","            div = det(xdiff, ydiff)\n","            if div == 0:\n","                continue\n","            d = (det(*line1), det(*line2))\n","            x = det(d, xdiff) / div\n","            y = det(d, ydiff) / div\n","            if min(line1[0][0], line1[1][0]) <= x <= max(line1[0][0], line1[1][0]) and min(line1[0][1], line1[1][1]) <= y <= max(line1[0][1], line1[1][1]):\n","                if min(line2[0][0], line2[1][0]) <= x <= max(line2[0][0], line2[1][0]) and min(line2[0][1], line2[1][1]) <= y <= max(line2[0][1], line2[1][1]):\n","                    intersections.append((x, y))\n","    return intersections\n","\n","def calculate_levels_and_discrepancy(lines):\n","    levels = defaultdict(int)\n","    for line in lines:\n","        (x1, y1), (x2, y2) = line  # Desempaquetar las coordenadas de inicio y fin de la línea\n","        for x, y in line:  # Iterar sobre los puntos de la línea actual, no sobre todas las líneas\n","            if (x1 < x < x2 and y < y1) or (x1 < x < x2 and y < y2):\n","                levels[(x, y)] += 1\n","    discrepancy = sum(levels.values())\n","    return levels, discrepancy\n","\n","def main():\n","    num_lines = int(input(\"Ingrese el número de líneas aleatorias a generar: \"))\n","    lines = []\n","    for i in range(num_lines):\n","        x1, y1, x2, y2 = np.random.rand(4) * 10\n","        lines.append(((x1, y1), (x2, y2)))\n","\n","    intersections = calculate_intersection(lines)\n","    draw_lines(lines, intersections)\n","\n","    levels, discrepancy = calculate_levels_and_discrepancy(lines)\n","    print(\"Niveles:\", levels)\n","    print(\"Discrepancia:\", discrepancy)\n","\n","if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n","    main()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":776},"id":"R748uZupRtTF","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1713436212590,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":4534,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"}},"outputId":"2680c80f-f6f1-43e9-832b-af994513f0c6"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Ingrese el número de líneas aleatorias a generar: 55\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Niveles: defaultdict(<class 'int'>, {})\n","Discrepancia: 0\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Detección de Intersecciones entre Líneas en 2D\n","\n","## Descripción:Este código genera un conjunto de líneas aleatorias en un plano 2D y detecta las intersecciones entre estas líneas. El usuario puede especificar el número de líneas que se generarán, y cada línea se dibujará entre dos puntos aleatorios en el plano. Además, se calculará el número de intersecciones y se mostrarán las coordenadas de las intersecciones. Los resultados se guardarán en un archivo CSV.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"UdHq3s6M1rbC"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from itertools import combinations\n","import pandas as pd\n","\n","def generate_lines(num_lines):\n","    lines = []\n","    for i in range(num_lines):\n","        x1, y1 = np.random.rand(2) * 10\n","        x2, y2 = np.random.rand(2) * 10\n","        lines.append(((x1, y1), (x2, y2)))\n","    return lines\n","\n","def plot_lines(lines):\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\n","    for line in lines:\n","        (x1, y1), (x2, y2) = line\n","        plt.plot([x1, x2], [y1, y2], marker='o')\n","    plt.xlabel('X')\n","    plt.ylabel('Y')\n","    plt.title('Líneas en 2D')\n","    plt.grid(True)\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","def calculate_intersections(lines):\n","    intersections = []\n","    for line1, line2 in combinations(lines, 2):\n","        (x1, y1), (x2, y2) = line1\n","        (x3, y3), (x4, y4) = line2\n","\n","        denominator = ((y4 - y3) * (x2 - x1)) - ((x4 - x3) * (y2 - y1))\n","\n","        if denominator == 0:\n","            continue\n","\n","        ua = (((x4 - x3) * (y1 - y3)) - ((y4 - y3) * (x1 - x3))) / denominator\n","        ub = (((x2 - x1) * (y1 - y3)) - ((y2 - y1) * (x1 - x3))) / denominator\n","\n","        if 0 <= ua <= 1 and 0 <= ub <= 1:\n","            x = x1 + ua * (x2 - x1)\n","            y = y1 + ua * (y2 - y1)\n","            intersections.append((x, y))\n","    return intersections\n","\n","def main():\n","    num_lines = int(input(\"Ingrese el número de líneas a generar: \"))\n","    lines = generate_lines(num_lines)\n","    plot_lines(lines)\n","    intersections = calculate_intersections(lines)\n","    print(\"Número de intersecciones:\", len(intersections))\n","    print(\"Coordenadas de las intersecciones:\", intersections)\n","\n","    # Crear un DataFrame con los datos de las intersecciones\n","    df = pd.DataFrame(intersections, columns=['X', 'Y'])\n","    print(\"\\nDataFrame con las intersecciones:\")\n","    print(df)\n","\n","    # Guardar el DataFrame como archivo CSV\n","    df.to_csv('intersecciones.csv', index=False)\n","    print(\"\\nEl DataFrame se ha guardado como 'intersecciones.csv'\")\n","\n","if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n","    main()\n","\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"n0-m0zOZbnnK","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1713436685508,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":4450,"user":{"displayName":"PEDRO LUIS PEREZ BARAHONA","userId":"16526492446743362157"}},"outputId":"dde668b0-5e00-42e1-e73c-883284599f3d"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Ingrese el número de líneas a generar: 22\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Número de intersecciones: 40\n","Coordenadas de las intersecciones: [(8.769977070229942, 5.058184468478474), (8.126066690541895, 5.048934559796147), (8.25167760731423, 5.050738987161039), (8.223866077248841, 9.067968417858665), (8.664345235567215, 5.833779247961046), (4.247167814802207, 5.223688709551847), (5.302492593002134, 4.395084506292916), (5.281084696364281, 4.4118932399676), (4.933331479243649, 4.684936935477593), (3.1818266919972404, 3.753676241851399), (3.2258945057185393, 3.3283656790672955), (3.2922656428503414, 2.6877996218384492), (3.2349815738062264, 3.2406638913890102), (4.958703636913075, 9.558543344073044), (7.764647673274167, 5.717441997371871), (1.6712516711374188, 1.6693071449238213), (2.920022711700486, 3.392425646251996), (2.521162532335621, 2.8420578588978147), (2.807605505542141, 3.237306604004087), (2.1275036484060283, 2.298867086468124), (4.109872341956384, 6.480712825762031), (1.5993306525424469, 1.84970992627456), (4.895681130230084, 7.49548378296815), (4.949759154777956, 7.521034304961507), (6.062913974333422, 8.046972279524262), (5.2872807962125385, 4.362318621114898), (4.667127816389863, 3.026522356496489), (4.406399231050925, 2